From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:48:20 +0800
Subject: cli/server: Web Push for the web app

The server keeps a VAPID key and the browsers' push subscriptions in
<data>/web-push.json and serves /api/ocelot/push (key, subscription,
test, presence). It follows its own event stream and pushes when a
top-level session finishes (the reply as the body) or fails, or a session
asks for a permission or an answer (under its top-level session). Every
open web app reports whether it is in use (visible, focused, touched in
the last 3 minutes); while one is, nothing is pushed. Payloads are
encrypted per RFC 8291 and signed per RFC 8292 with node:crypto, no new
dependency. A 404/410 from the push service drops the subscription.

Nothing is pushed until a browser subscribes. Not for a TUI's private
stdio server.

Ocelot-Patch: cli/web-push

